## Who is a preventive stay suitable for?

- **40+** — the age at which it pays to monitor blood pressure, weight and metabolic markers regularly
- **Sedentary occupations** — programmers, managers, drivers
- **Family history** — diabetes, hypertension or cancer in the family
- **Long-term stress** — a stay can improve sleep and fatigue, but it does not replace psychotherapy or psychiatric care
- **After an illness** — convalescence under medical supervision, for example [after Covid](/en/magazine/post-covid-rehabilitation)

If you are being treated for a chronic condition, consult your doctor before booking. Acute infections and fever are among the general contraindications to spa care.

## What the studies say about preventive stays

There are fewer studies on preventive stays for healthy people than on the treatment of specific diseases. Those that exist, however, show measurable things:

- **Stress, sleep and fatigue.** In a Lithuanian randomised trial with 373 adults with high stress levels, spa programmes of just 6–11 days improved fatigue, sleep and quality of life, and the effect lasted 6 months; balneotherapy worked better than a stay in nature alone ([Rapolienė et al., 2025](https://consensus.app/papers/details/9b8af91815645dce946c8b1e5c4f8834/), *Int J Biometeorol*). Among 362 "sub-healthy" adults in China, five months of regular bathing led to fewer sleep disturbances and less psychological stress than in the control group; the study was not randomised and relies on questionnaires ([Yang et al., 2018](https://consensus.app/papers/details/5da141d1b4205f63a3d401732e517a95/), *Int J Biometeorol*).
- **Habits that last.** In a French randomised trial with 228 spa patients, 81% of those who received coaching and an app at the spa were meeting physical activity recommendations a year later, compared with 67% in the control group; the data were self-reported ([Fillol et al., 2021](https://consensus.app/papers/details/9846c5e2ca6e51919ee22de7f113a384/), *J Med Internet Res*).
- **Fewer painkillers.** In people who already have joint or back pain, randomised trials showed lower analgesic use after a spa cure: in 80 patients with knee osteoarthritis after two weeks of peloids and baths, still evident after 9 months ([Fioravanti et al., 2010](https://consensus.app/papers/details/117ceeafb8b45fcb8ed8113fbdbc701c/), *Am J Phys Med Rehabil*), and in 121 patients with chronic low back pain after 6 months ([Constant et al., 1995](https://consensus.app/papers/details/c40f2f7cb25b57788b900083c0151358/), *J Rheumatol*). Both studies were unblinded and from a single centre.

You can read more about what a spa stay can do for resilience and sleep in the article [Prevention and resilience](/en/magazine/immunity-prevention-spa).

## Marienbad and prevention: what is unique

Marienbad has more than 40 mineral springs of varying composition within the town. This makes an **individualised drinking cure** possible: the spa physician selects the spring, the dose and the time of day according to your health profile.

Natural CO₂ gas from the Maria Spring is used in [CO₂ baths and dry gas baths](/en/co2-therapy). These are treatments that spa physicians traditionally prescribe for patients with disorders of the circulatory system, and whether they are included in a preventive programme is decided by the physician according to your condition and contraindications.

And [climate therapy](/en/climate-therapy) — medically prescribed forest walks with a defined gradient — is prevention that requires no equipment at all. Just the forest, the air and movement.

## When to come and for how long

The best time for a preventive stay is **whenever you feel well**. That is precisely when prevention makes the most sense.

A preventive stay is not covered by health insurance; you come as a self-paying guest. You therefore choose the length of your stay yourself in consultation with the spa physician, most often 1–3 weeks. Expert correspondence regards 2–3 weeks with 10–21 treatments as the norm for spa treatment ([Karagülle and Karagülle, 2021](https://consensus.app/papers/details/14ac08e16e2d5bbb804b6330ab17303b/), *Int J Biometeorol*); shorter stays are regenerative rather than therapeutic in character.

Read more about [planning your stay](/en/practical-info) and [accommodation](/en/accommodation) in Marienbad.
